DESCRIPTION: \nOpen to all students!\nCurious about what to expect at a ca
 reer fair? Stop by this interactive mock career fair to practice navigati
 ng the experience in a low-pressure setting. Staff from IU Career Centers
  and campus offices will serve as mock employers\, giving you the chance 
 to practice introductions\, ask questions\, and learn strategies for maki
 ng the most of a career fair.\nYou’ll leave with practical tips\, greater
  confidence\, and a better idea of what to expect when attending a real c
 areer fair.\nThis is a drop-in\, in-person event\, so come by whenever it
  works for your schedule!\n\nHosted by: Asian Culture Center\, Accessible
  Educational Services\, Center for Veteran and Military Students\, Colleg
 e of Arts and Sciences\, First Nations Educational and Cultural Center\, 
 First Generation and Limited/Low-Income Programs\, Groups Scholars Progra
 m\, IU 21st Century Scholars Program\, Jewish Culture Center\, Jacobs Sch
 ool of Music\, Luddy Consulting Association\, LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, La 
 Casa/Latino Cultural Center\, Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center\, School
  of Social Work\, School of Education\, Undergraduate Education\n\nAdditi
 onal Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12
 790964
