X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:GroupBusiness
CATEGORIES:Academic/Career
DESCRIPTION:\nBreaking Into High Finance as an International\, with Julian
  Croonenberghs (Hg)\nHow does an international student land a role in hig
 h finance\, and what does the job actually look like once you’re there? J
 oin EBA for an informal coffee chat with Julian Croonenberghs of Hg\, one
  of Europe’s leading private equity investors in software and services.\n
 Julian will open with a short presentation on his path into finance\, wha
 t his day-to-day work involves\, and what he’s learned about recruiting a
 cross Europe and the US. The rest of the session is yours: bring your que
 stions on internships\, networking\, visas and work authorization\, inter
 view prep\, and how to stand out when you’re not from the “standard” pipe
 line.\nWhether you’re an international student aiming for Wall Street or 
 the City\, or an American student curious about a career in Europe\, this
  is a rare chance to hear it straight from someone who’s done it.\n\nHost
 ed by: European Business Association\n\nAdditional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12933895
DTEND:20261104T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261104T223000Z
LOCATION:Global & International Studies\, GA 4067
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:EBA X Hg Capital
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12933895
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12933895
X-HOSTS:European Business Association
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Social Event
DESCRIPTION:\nImprove your English-speaking skills and learn from native s
 peakers who are eager to share their knowledge of the language. \n\n\nSes
 sions focus on topics like slang\, holidays\, and American culture in gen
 eral. No reservations are necessary—stop by and join us anytime. We meet 
 twice a week during the semester on Mondays and Wednesdays. For Fall 2026
 \, PET will begin on September 16th\, with all sessions held in-person at
  the Ferguson International Center\, Room 423.\nIs English your first lan
 guage? Have you been speaking it so long that it may as well be? Become a
  tutor and help international students at IUB become more comfortable wri
 ting\, reading\, and speaking English. Engage in IU’s global network and 
 make connections that last a lifetime.\nYou can also sign up to practice 
 your conversational English skills as a participant. Register and join th
 e email list HERE. \n\n\nHosted by: \n\nAdditional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12670140
DTEND:20261105T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261104T230000Z
