DESCRIPTION:From Hello Kitty’s global empire to Labubu and K-pop idols\, "
 cute" has become one of East Asia's most powerful and contested cultural 
 exports. This session frames “cuteness” as an aesthetic category\, tracin
 g kawaii culture’s root in postwar Japan\, and its journey into global po
 p culture. A harder question follows: What gets flattened or fetishized w
 hen cuteness travels across cultures? This event will be facilitated by H
 aoxuan Gao\, a Sociology PhD student at IU Bloomington who studies cultur
 e\, modernity\, and social psychology. \n \nAll Indiana University events
 \, groups\, activities\, and educational\, cultural\, and historical obse
 rvances welcome all IU students and other members of the Indiana Universi
 ty community.\n\nHosted by: Asian Culture Center\n\nAdditional Informatio
 n can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12476676
DTEND:20261105T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261105T220000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACC's Over A Cup of Tea presents Aesthetics of the Cute: Globaliza
 tion of East Asian Kawaii Culture by Haoxuan Gao
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12476676
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12476676
X-HOSTS:Asian Culture Center
END:VEVENT
