DESCRIPTION:Join Groups Scholars in welcoming the President of the Souther
 n Region of IU Health to campus on Wednesday\, November 11\, 2026 at 6:00
  pm in Wells library\, room 0026. \n \nDenzil Ross is the president of th
 e southern region of IU Health\, where he leads strategic and operational
  avenues for IU Health Bloomington\, Bedford\, Morgan\, and Paoli Hospita
 ls\, along with over 60 ambulatory clinics and joint ventures encompassin
 g more than 5\,000 team members in seven counties.\nBefore joining IU Hea
 lth\, Mr. Ross served as the chief executive officer for Northwest Medica
 l Center Houghton in Tucson\, Arizona\, a 145-bed facility he helped open
  during the COVID-19 pandemic. His previous leadership roles include Chie
 f Operating Officer and Lead Administrator for Lovelace Medical Center an
 d Heart Hospital of New Mexico\, and Chief Operating Officer and Ethics a
 nd Compliance Officer at Metropolitan Methodist in San Antonio\, TX. Mr. 
 Ross is a fellow of the American College of Healthcare Executives and a c
 o-founder of the Kansas City Regional Chapter of the National Association
  of Health Service Executives. \nMr. Ross earned a Master of Business Adm
 inistration with an emphasis in Healthcare and Health Services Management
  and a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science\, with an emphasis in Syst
 ems Analysis\, from Park University in Parkville\, Missouri.\n\nHosted by
 : Groups Scholars Program\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: http
 s://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12874267
DTEND:20261112T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261111T230000Z
