DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to join the ACC in discussing Interpreter of M
 aladies\, a 1999 short story collection by Indian-American author Jhumpa 
 Lahiri.\n \nDrawing from Lahiri's own experiences as a London-born daught
 er of Bengali immigrants\, the nine stories explore the longing\, transfo
 rmation\, and community of making a home in a new place. Each session wil
 l cover 3 out of the collection's 9 total stories\, so feel free to drop 
 in for any of the three meetings.\n \nPizza will be served\, and limited 
 copies of the book will be available to those who sign up ~ first come/fi
 rst serve. For more information\, please reach out to ACC volunteer and b
 ook club moderator Cheryl Nong\, PhD student in social psychology\, at ac
 c@iu.edu.\n \nAll Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, and e
 ducational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all IU student
 s and other members of the Indiana University community.\n\nHosted by: As
 ian Culture Center\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://bei
 nvolved.indiana.edu/event/12705041
DTEND:20261112T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261112T220000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACC Book Club features The Interpreter of Maladies by Jhumpa Lahiri
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12705041
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12705041
X-HOSTS:Asian Culture Center
