BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
DESCRIPTION: \nArtificial intelligence is changing how the United States f
 ights\, spies\, and defends itself\, and the laws that govern national se
 curity were not written for it. The Pentagon is racing to put AI to work 
 in intelligence analysis\, cyber operations\, and military planning\, and
  it has clashed with a leading AI developer over who gets to set the limi
 ts on how these tools are used. China is pouring resources into the same 
 technologies\, and Chinese state hackers have already burrowed deep into 
 American telecommunications networks. Meanwhile\, Congress and the courts
  are struggling to decide what rules should govern a technology that move
 s faster than they do.\nThe Alexander Hamilton Society at Indiana Univers
 ity welcomes Jamil N. Jaffer\, founder and executive director of the Nati
 onal Security Institute at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law S
 chool\, for a conversation on these questions. Jaffer has shaped national
  security law from the White House\, the Justice Department\, the House I
 ntelligence Committee\, and the Senate Foreign Relations Committee\, and 
 today he invests in the defense and cybersecurity technologies at the cen
 ter of this debate. He will discuss where America stands in the global AI
  competition\, how AI is reshaping cyber offense and defense\, what the P
 entagon’s embrace of AI means for U.S. defense policy\, and how national 
 security law will need to change to keep up.\nThe evening opens with rema
 rks from Jaffer\, followed by a moderated conversation and audience Q&A. 
 Students\, faculty\, and the public interested in foreign policy\, defens
 e\, cybersecurity\, technology\, and law are especially encouraged to att
 end.\n----\nJamil N. Jaffer is founder and executive director of George M
 ason University’s National Security Institute and a venture partner at Pa
 ladin Capital Group. He served as Associate Counsel to President George W
 . Bush\, Senior Counsel to the House Intelligence Committee\, and Chief C
 ounsel to the Senate Foreign Relations Committee\, and he clerked for Jus
 tice Neil Gorsuch at the Supreme Court. He recently served on DHS’s Cyber
  Safety Review Board.\n\nHosted by: The Alexander Hamilton Society at Ind
 iana University \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinv
 olved.indiana.edu/event/12925781
DTEND:20261113T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261112T230000Z
LOCATION:Global International Studies Building\, GA 0001
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Intelligence Race: AI\, Cyber\, and the Future of National Sec
 urity Law
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12925781
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12925781
X-HOSTS:The Alexander Hamilton Society at Indiana University
END:VEVENT
