X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:Arts
CATEGORIES:Performance
CATEGORIES:Concert
CATEGORIES:Arts & Humanities
DESCRIPTION:Native American Voices is a music and storytelling presentatio
 n that highlights Native American voices in both contemporary composition
  and traditional storytelling.  The program opens with three short works 
 written by Indigenous youth through the South Dakota Symphony Orchestra's
  Lakota Music Project Composition Academy\, an initiative that empowers N
 ative American students to share their experiences through original compo
 sition.\n \nThe featured work is Moonstrike by Chickasaw composer Jerod I
 mpichchaachaaha' Tate\, one of today's leading Native American classical 
 composers. Written to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the Apollo 11 m
 oon landing\, the work combines string quartet music with Native stories 
 about the moon\, illuminating the rich storytelling traditions that have 
 been passed through generations of Indigenous communities.\n \nA unique a
 spect of this presentation is the participation of narrator Mike Pace\, a
  Lenape educator and former cultural interpreter at Conner Prairie.  Mike
  brings a deeply personal perspective to the stories through his connecti
 ons to Indiana's Native history\, including family ties to Chief Anderson
 \, for whom the city of Anderson is named\, and to the Conner family asso
 ciated with Conner Prairie.  His narration provides audiences with an aut
 hentic and engaging connection to the cultural themes explored throughout
  the program.\n\nHosted by: First Nations Educational and Cultural Center
 \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.ed
 u/event/12843556
DTEND:20261115T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261115T190000Z
GEO:39.166900;-86.524760
LOCATION:Cook Center at Maxwell Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Native American Voices presents The Lakota Music Project and Moons
 trike
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12843556
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12843556
X-HOSTS:First Nations Educational and Cultural Center
END:VEVENT
