BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:Arts
CATEGORIES:Speaker
CATEGORIES:Arts & Humanities
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Native Heritage Month\, join us for an inspi
 ring afternoon with Susan Charlesworth\, an award-winning basket weaver a
 nd enrolled citizen of the Choctaw Nation of Oklahoma.\n \n<!--TgQPHd|||[
 ]-->\nSusan is an award-winning basket weaver who first began weaving in 
 2005\, when she entered her baskets into the Choctaw Nation Annual Labor 
 Day Festival and Art Show. Susan has continued to receive awards at multi
 ple Native art markets\, including the Eiteljorg Indian Market & Festival
 . Susan is a retired CNA and social service consultant with a master’s de
 gree in social work and an avid volunteer with the Alzheimer’s Associatio
 n. She now serves as an Alzheimer’s Association Community Educator in Ind
 ianapolis.\n \nEvent Timeline:• 12:00 PM – 1:00 PM: Lunch served on a fir
 st come first serve basis.• 1:00 PM – 2:00 PM: Artist Talk & Presentation
  by Susan Charlesworth<!--TgQPHd|||[]-->\n• 2:00 PM – 4:00 PM: Art making
 /museum activities with museum staff \n\nHosted by: First Nations Educati
 onal and Cultural Center\, Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art\n\nAddi
 tional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/
 12874711
DTEND:20261118T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261118T170000Z
GEO:39.168880;-86.519810
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Eiteljorg Artist In Residence Visiting Lecture: Susan Charlesworth
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12874711
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12874711
X-HOSTS:Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art
END:VEVENT
