BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:GroupBusiness
CATEGORIES:Business Meeting
CATEGORIES:Academic/Career
DESCRIPTION:Step into the role of a consultant and design an AI-powered gr
 owth engine for a growing protein supplement brand.\nOur client is a smal
 ler supplement company competing against much larger players with bigger 
 marketing budgets. To scale\, they want to outsource marketing to partner
  agencies. The catch is that finding\, evaluating\, and negotiating with 
 those agencies is slow and manual. Your team’s job is to build the plan f
 or an AI infrastructure that can identify marketing partners\, structure 
 deals\, and manage those relationships efficiently.\nWorking in teams\, y
 ou will:\n\nAssess the company’s current operations and where AI fits\nDe
 sign the infrastructure: tools\, data flows\, and decision points\nBuild 
 an implementation roadmap covering timeline\, cost\, and risk\nPresent yo
 ur recommendation to a panel of judges\n\nNo technical background require
 d. This event is built for anyone interested in strategy\, operations\, c
 onsulting\, or how AI is reshaping business decisions. It’s a chance to p
 ractice case work\, think like an implementer rather than just an ideator
 \, and connect with peers who share your interest in AI.\n\nHosted by: AI
  in Business Society\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://b
 einvolved.indiana.edu/event/12927077
DTEND:20261120T014500Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261119T234500Z
LOCATION:Global & International Studies\, GA 1100
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:AI Industry Case Simulation Night #1
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12927077
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12927077
X-HOSTS:AI in Business Society
END:VEVENT
