BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
CATEGORIES:Emotional Wellness
CATEGORIES:Social Wellness
DESCRIPTION:Feeling well is an ongoing journey - join us on the first Mond
 ay of every month to work on your wellness!\nOur workshops are engaging a
 nd interactive - no lectures here. You will learn new skills and have a c
 hance to share your concerns\, if you choose. We are here to help you dev
 elop skills that will take you from IU into the future.\nSeptember: Stres
 s Management\nBuild your stress management strengths! Understand more abo
 ut how stress can impact your life and what you can do to take control.\n
 October: Time Management\nLife doesn't have to be a crush - learn how to 
 manage your time and get some back for yourself\nNovember: Supporting Eac
 h Other\nHow can we help each other as we navigate challenges? Learn how 
 to identify when a friend might need help and steps to take to start the 
 conversation.\nDecember: Mindfulness and Meditation\nLearn five-minute me
 ditations\, and try out relaxation stations to learn skills to build your
  chill.\n \n\nHosted by: Health Promotion\n\nAdditional Information can b
 e found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12641333
DTEND:20261207T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261207T170000Z
GEO:39.172430;-86.515960
LOCATION:Wellness House
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:First Mondays Wellness Workshops
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12641333
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12641333
X-HOSTS:Health Promotion
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:CommunityService
DESCRIPTION:Mindfulness in the Meadow is an outdoor workshop to aid in lea
 rning mindfulness practices to support well-being. This is a drop-in supp
 ort group that does not require students to sign up to participate. This 
 is an introductory level of experience for students who may be new to min
 dfulness practices or are wanting to enhance the skills they may already 
 possess in a non-committal support space. The focus is to increase comfor
 t by engaging with mindfulness interventions and self-care while engaging
  with a natural enirvonment!\n\nHosted by: Counseling and Psychological S
 ervices (CAPS)\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvol
 ved.indiana.edu/event/12660478
DTEND:20261207T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261207T200000Z
LOCATION:Dunn Meadow 1 (West side and concrete pad)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mindfulness in the Meadow
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12660478
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12660478
X-HOSTS:Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:Social
CATEGORIES:Social Event
CATEGORIES:Arts & Humanities
CATEGORIES:Tradition & Community
CATEGORIES:Engage & Thrive - Community
CATEGORIES:Campus-Wide Event
DESCRIPTION:Once associated with older generations\, Mahjong has now found
  a new home among the young. Social clubs have emerged dedicated to playi
 ng Mahjong to reconnect with culture and\, more importantly\, to foster n
 ew friendships. At the ACC\, we offer a casual and informal Mahjong exper
 ience\, perfect for those looking to learn the game\, take a break from t
 he digital world\, and most importantly\, meet new friends in person. You
  do not need to be an expert to join us\, just bring your enthusiasm and 
 a willingness to learn!\n \nAll Indiana University events\, groups\, acti
 vities\, and educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome 
 all IU students and other members of the Indiana University community.\n\
 nHosted by: Asian Culture Center\n\nAdditional Information can be found a
 t: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12470853
DTEND:20261207T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052043Z
DTSTART:20261207T210000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Asian Cultures Around Campus: Mahjong Mondays
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12470853
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12470853
X-HOSTS:Asian Culture Center
